@node Overview
@chapter Overview

@samp{pdf-tools-extras.el} extends the @samp{pdf-tools} package with commands and functions that improve everyday PDF workflows in Emacs. The built-in @samp{pdf-tools} is excellent for viewing and annotating PDFs@comma{} but certain operations---opening a PDF in an external viewer at the current page@comma{} extracting all text@comma{} adapting the display to the active theme---require additional code. This package fills those gaps.

The main areas of functionality are:

@itemize
@item
PDF conversion: extracting text from PDFs via @samp{pdftotext} (@ref{PDF conversion, , PDF conversion}).
@item
Theme integration: automatically toggling midnight mode to match the active Modus theme (@ref{Theme integration, , Theme integration}).
@item
Text operations: counting words@comma{} copying text with DWIM behavior@comma{} and enhanced highlight annotations (@ref{Text operations, , Text operations}).
@item
External interaction: opening the PDF in an external viewer at the current page@comma{} toggling @samp{writeroom-mode}@comma{} deleting the file (@ref{External interaction, , External interaction}).
@item
Ebib integration: jumping from a PDF to the corresponding Bib@TeX{} entry (@ref{Ebib integration, , Ebib integration}).
@item
Word lookup via double-click (@ref{Word lookup, , Word lookup}).
@end itemize

The package depends on @samp{pdf-tools} and @samp{johnson}@comma{} and optionally integrates with @samp{modus-themes}@comma{} @samp{writeroom-mode}@comma{} and @samp{ebib-extras.el}.

