@node PDF conversion
@section PDF conversion

@vindex pdf-tools-extras-pdftotext-executable
The variable @code{pdf-tools-extras-pdftotext-executable} holds the path to the @samp{pdftotext} executable (default @samp{"pdftotext"}). Customize it if the executable is installed in a non-standard location.

@findex pdf-tools-extras-convert-pdf
The function @code{pdf-tools-extras-convert-pdf} converts a PDF file to plain text. It accepts a SOURCE file path and an optional DESTINATION@. When DESTINATION is non-nil@comma{} the text is written to that file; otherwise@comma{} the text is returned as a string. This is the main entry point for PDF text extraction and is used by other packages such as @samp{read-aloud-extras.el}. It has an @samp{;;;###autoload} cookie@comma{} so external packages can call it without requiring @samp{pdf-tools-extras} first.

@findex pdf-tools-extras--run-pdftotext
Internally@comma{} @code{pdf-tools-extras--run-pdftotext} runs the @samp{pdftotext} executable on a SOURCE file@comma{} writing to OUTPUT (a file path or @samp{"-"} for stdout). It accepts an optional EXTRA-ARGS list for additional flags such as margin settings. It signals an error if @samp{pdftotext} is not installed.

@node Theme integration
@section Theme integration

@findex pdf-tools-extras-apply-theme
Reading a bright-white PDF in a dark Emacs theme is unpleasant@comma{} and @samp{pdf-tools} provides @code{pdf-view-midnight-minor-mode} to invert colors. The function @code{pdf-tools-extras-apply-theme} inspects the currently active Modus theme and enables midnight mode if the theme has a dark background@comma{} or disables it for a light background. This function is intended to be called from a theme-change hook so that PDFs automatically adapt when you switch themes.

Internally@comma{} it calls @code{modus-themes-get-current-theme} and reads the @samp{:background-mode} property from the theme's metadata to determine whether the theme is dark or light.

@node Word lookup
@section Word lookup

@vindex pdf-tools-extras-sel-mode-map
@findex pdf-tools-extras-lookup-word-at-mouse
The minor mode @code{pdf-tools-extras-sel-mode} binds double-click (@samp{[double-mouse-1]}) to @code{pdf-tools-extras-lookup-word-at-mouse}. This command selects the word under the mouse cursor in the PDF@comma{} highlights it@comma{} and looks it up with @code{johnson-lookup}. If no word is found at the click position@comma{} it signals a user error.

